('116.16.b.3.A',3,'Which is a key element of throwing?','["dropping the ball", "closing your eyes", "follow-through", "hiding"]'::jsonb,2,'Follow-through improves accuracy.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.A',3,'Transferring your body weight when throwing means you shift weight from your...','["head to your foot", "front foot to your elbow", "hand to your ear", "back foot to your front foot"]'::jsonb,3,'Weight shifts forward for power.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.B',3,'Catching a ball above your waist uses...','["thumbs together", "fingers pointing down", "elbows together", "pinkies together"]'::jsonb,0,'Thumbs together catch high balls.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.B',3,'Catching a ball below your waist uses...','["only one finger", "pinkies together and fingers pointing down", "thumbs together", "palms up high"]'::jsonb,1,'Pinkies together catch low balls.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.C',3,'Dribbling with your non-dominant hand while changing direction helps you...','["stand still", "forget the ball", "improve control with both hands", "ignore your team"]'::jsonb,2,'Practice improves both hands.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.D',3,'When dribbling with a partner and changing speed and direction, you should...','["kick it hard", "run in circles", "let it go", "keep the ball close and watch your partner"]'::jsonb,3,'Awareness helps with control.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.E',3,'A key element of kicking is to...','["transfer your weight from your back foot to your front foot", "hop only", "stay in one place", "kick with your eyes closed"]'::jsonb,0,'Weight transfer adds power.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.E',3,'For a strong kick, your non-kicking foot should be planted...','["on top of the ball", "beside the ball", "far behind you", "in the air"]'::jsonb,1,'A planted foot gives balance.','original'),
('116.16.b.3.F',3,'Overhead volleying means you hit the ball with your...','["elbows", "feet", "fingertips above your forehead", "knees"]'::jsonb,2,'Overhead sets use fingertips.','original'),
